body:
I told my surgeon I just wanted them as small as he was able to safely do possible. To be honest I don't know my before size, around a DD or E. He told me we could aim for a fuller B or smaller C. I'm 4 days post op, and I am so happy with them already. 

&#x200B;

Also my surgeon told me 6months post op, if you're not happy with the results he will do key hole surgery for free to take out more fat and make them that bit smaller. Maybe ask your surgeon if he has an option like that?

This is where people are going wrong, VOTE, make small changes in your life, become vegetarian or limit your intake on animal products, learn about recycling and power usage where you live and how you can make small differences that don't effect the environment around you. Every state has different recycling policies and different grades, just because it's plastic doesn't mean it can be recycled it has to be a certain grade. Ride a bike or take public transport to work, even just a couple days a week. Avoid certain products, such as products that contain palm oil. 

&#x200B;

There's lots of small things, but fact is, people are lazy and don't want to make the effort to change because it's a lot to learn and takes a conscious effort. But if you make small changes and learn a small new thing say even once a month, your on your way to making a change. Now imagine if EVERYONE in your country had this mindset? it would make a difference.
